            "content": "# use-ai Feature Requirements & Test Coverage\n\nThis document lists all features in requirements format with test coverage status.\n\n**Legend:**\n- ✅ TESTED - Feature has test coverage\n- ❌ NOT TESTED - Feature exists but lacks tests\n- ⚠️ PARTIAL - Feature has some test coverage but gaps remain\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Package (AG-UI Protocol)\n\n### Protocol Event Types\n\n1. ✅ The system emits RUN_STARTED events with threadId, runId, optional parentRunId, and optional input\n2. ✅ The system emits RUN_FINISHED events with threadId, runId, and optional result\n3. ✅ The system emits RUN_ERROR events with message string and optional error code\n4. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_START events with messageId and optional role\n5. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT events with messageId and delta string\n6. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_END events with messageId\n7. ❌ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_CHUNK events with optional messageId, role, and delta\n8. ❌ The system emits THINKING_TEXT_MESSAGE_START events without requiring messageId\n9. ❌ The system emits THINKING_TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT events with delta\n10. ❌ The system emits THINKING_TEXT_MESSAGE_END events\n11. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_START events with toolCallId, toolCallName, and optional parentMessageId\n12. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_ARGS events with toolCallId and delta\n13. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_END events with toolCallId\n14. ❌ The system emits TOOL_CALL_CHUNK events with optional toolCallId, toolCallName, parentMessageId, and delta\n15. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_RESULT events with messageId, toolCallId, and stringified content\n16. ✅ The system emits STATE_SNAPSHOT events with application state\n17. ❌ The system emits STATE_DELTA events with array of state changes\n18. ✅ The system emits MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT events with all message objects\n19. ❌ The system emits ACTIVITY_SNAPSHOT events with messageId, activityType, content, and replace flag\n20. ❌ The system emits ACTIVITY_DELTA events with messageId, activityType, and JSON patch operations\n21. ❌ The system emits RAW events with arbitrary event data and optional source\n22. ❌ The system emits CUSTOM events with name and arbitrary value\n23. ❌ The system emits STEP_STARTED events with stepName identifier\n24. ❌ The system emits STEP_FINISHED events with stepName identifier\n25. ⚠️ The system supports optional timestamps on all events\n\n### Message Types\n\n26. ✅ The system supports developer messages with role, id, and content string\n27. ✅ The system supports system messages with role, id, and content string\n28. ✅ The system supports assistant messages with role, id, optional content, and optional toolCalls array\n29. ✅ The system supports user messages with role, id, and content as string or array\n30. ✅ The system supports tool messages with role, id, toolCallId, content, and optional error\n31. ❌ The system supports activity messages with role, id, activityType, and content record\n32. ❌ The system supports binary content with mimeType, optional id, url, data, and filename\n\n### Tool Definitions\n\n33. ✅ The system defines tool definitions with name, description, and JSON Schema parameters\n34. ✅ The system supports optional confirmationRequired flag on tools\n35. ✅ Tool definitions contain parameters as JSON Schema object type\n\n### Client-to-Server Messages\n\n36. ✅ The protocol supports run_agent message type\n37. ✅ The protocol supports tool_result message type\n38. ✅ The protocol supports abort_run message type\n39. ❌ The protocol supports run_workflow message type (use-ai extension)\n\n### RunAgentInput Structure\n\n40. ✅ RunAgentInput requires threadId identifier\n41. ✅ RunAgentInput requires runId identifier\n42. ✅ RunAgentInput supports optional parentRunId\n43. ✅ RunAgentInput requires messages array\n44. ✅ RunAgentInput requires tools array\n45. ✅ RunAgentInput requires context array with value and description pairs\n46. ✅ RunAgentInput supports optional s