int configurations from environment variables\n350. ✅ The start.ts script reads environment variables: PORT, RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS, RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS, LOG_FORMAT\n351. ✅ The system listens on configured port with WebSocket support\n\n### Pattern Matching\n\n352. ✅ The system uses picomatch-based pattern matching for MCP header configuration\n353. ✅ The system supports exact string matches with highest priority\n354. ✅ The system supports glob patterns for wildcard matching\n355. ✅ The system supports multi-wildcard patterns\n356. ✅ The matchesPattern function returns true for exact matches before attempting glob matching\n357. ✅ The findMatch function returns first matching pattern value with exact matches having priority\n\n### Event Emission and Socket.IO\n\n358. ✅ The system checks if socket is connected before emitting events\n359. ✅ The system emits events via socket.emit('event', event)\n360. ✅ The system sends all AG-UI events to clients via same 'event' channel\n\n### Server Lifecycle\n\n361. ✅ The system creates cleanup interval timer that runs at rate-limit window interval\n362. ✅ The system clears cleanup interval when closing server\n363. ✅ The system closes Socket.IO server on server.close()\n364. ✅ The system closes HTTP server on server.close()\n365. ✅ The system destroys all MCP endpoint providers on server.close()\n\n### Error Validation\n\n366. ✅ The system throws error if specified default agent name does not exist in agents map\n367. ✅ The error message lists available agent names when default agent is not found\n\n**Server Package Summary: 133/149 tested (89%)**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Workflows Plugin Package\n\n### WorkflowsPlugin Capabilities\n\n368. ❌ The system registers plugin named \"workflows\" that handles workflow execution requests\n369. ❌ The system registers message handler for messages of type \"run_workflow\"\n370. ❌ The system retrieves requested workflow runner by name from configured runners map\n371. ❌ The system emits RUN_ERROR 