ress callback receives updated tool call information after each execution\n   207→126. ❌ Tool execution errors are sent back to the workflow\n   208→\n   209→---\n   210→\n   211→## Protocol & Types\n   212→\n   213→### AG-UI Protocol\n   214→\n   215→127. ✅ The AG-UI protocol defines standardized event types for AI-UI communication\n   216→128. ✅ The protocol supports streaming text messages (TEXT_MESSAGE_START, _CONTENT, _END)\n   217→129. ✅ The protocol supports streaming tool calls (TOOL_CALL_START, _ARGS, _END)\n   218→130. ✅ The protocol supports run lifecycle events (RUN_STARTED, RUN_FINISHED, RUN_ERROR)\n   219→131. ✅ The protocol supports state snapshots (STATE_SNAPSHOT, MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT)\n   220→132. ❌ The protocol supports thinking messages (THINKING_TEXT_MESSAGE_*)\n   221→133. ❌ The protocol supports chunked messages (TEXT_MESSAGE_CHUNK, TOOL_CALL_CHUNK)\n   222→134. ❌ The protocol supports activity tracking (ACTIVITY_SNAPSHOT, ACTIVITY_DELTA)\n   223→135. ❌ The protocol supports step tracking (STEP_STARTED, STEP_FINISHED)\n   224→136. ❌ The protocol supports raw and custom events (RAW, CUSTOM)\n   225→137. ⚠️ All events support optional timestamps\n   226→\n   227→### Message Types\n   228→\n   229→138. ✅ The protocol supports user, assistant, system, developer, and tool message roles\n   230→139. ✅ Tool messages include tool call ID and result content\n   231→140. ✅ Assistant messages can include tool calls\n   232→141. ❌ The protocol supports activity messages for tracking activities\n   233→142. ❌ The protocol supports binary content in messages (images, files, etc.)\n   234→\n   235→### Type Safety & Exports\n   236→\n   237→143. ✅ The client exports TypeScript types for all hooks, components, and configurations\n   238→144. ✅ The server exports TypeScript types for agents, plugins, and configurations\n   239→145. ✅ The core package exports AG-UI protocol types\n   240→146. ✅ Zod is re-exported from the client package for schema definitions\n   24